  "interpretation": {
    "cache": "Actual same-process lock/unlock is distinct from process restart. Category grants remain isolated by origin and scope.",
    "concurrency": "Two overlapping public calls on the same granted100-satoshi origin; at most one may settle without fresh consent, exactly one is denied. No prompt/result can cross-bind.",
    "accounting": "Visible monthly usage is compared with independently verified signed external value plus fee. Aborted or terminally rejected actions cannot consume accepted-payment allowance. A held noSend action is explicitly compared before/after public abort; held reservation versus settled spend is reported separately instead of assuming broadcast.",
    "scope": "Permissions require actual trusted UI evidence. Reference wallets and simulated controls never supply native verdicts."
  },
